==English==

===Etymology===
{{back-form|en|grungy}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɡɹʌnd͡ʒ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-grunge.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌndʒ|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} [[dirt|Dirt]] or [[filth]], especially when difficult to [[clean]].
#: {{ux|en|The cinema floor was covered in '''grunge''' deposited by the crowds.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} The state of being [[filthy]]; [[grubbiness]].
#: {{ux|en|Chad used to work as a coal miner, but couldn't handle the constant '''grunge'''.}}
# {{lb|en|music genre}} A [[subgenre]] of [[alternative rock]], originating from Seattle, Washington, which melds [[punk]] and [[metal]].
#: {{ux|en|Alice liked to wear plaids and ripped jeans, and listen to '''grunge'''.}}

